        "original_id": "986b1dad-7ac6-5267-9ed9-8a5e48510dc2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Sparaxis, Campanula, Dierama pendulum\n- Taxonomy: Iridaceae, Campanulaceae, genera, species\n- Places: Cape Province, South Africa\n\nFacts:\n- Sparaxis, also called harlequin flower, is a genus in the family Iridaceae with about 13 species endemic to Cape Province, South Africa.\n- Campanula is one of several genera in the family Campanulaceae that share the common name bellflower.\n- Before its current placement, Dierama pendulum had been placed in various genera, including Ixia, Sparaxis, and Watsonia.",
